    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nHi, I'm using https://github.com/gbprod/substitute.nvim and notice I can't do \"si(\" to fill an empty pair, I see [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.ai/blob/640418aafb5a6e830eade483cdc2d4f0cd0e3f1a/lua/mini/ai.lua#L1024) has special rules for \"c\", \"d\" and mini.operators, can we add more?",
